  "actual_type_assessment": [
    {
      "scope": "XT02-01 / public ordinals1-16",
      "assessment": "All observation/predicate types are on the existing BinaryTree with arbitrary Type u payload. Constructor/min/max/subtraction sides have the intended Nat instances. Three map laws preserve independent Type u and Type v with only a label function, no injectivity or label structure. Completeness node form has equal maxima plus both recursive child premises; almost-complete child closure retains the parent premise. Definition meaning is assessed from full source, not inferred from printed codomain."
    },
    {
      "scope": "XT02-02 / public ordinals17-24",
      "assessment": "Universal capacities have no shape or nonempty premise. Equalities assume Complete; both strict inequalities assume Not Complete. Both iff statements express equality with the appropriate power at actual height/minimum, not mere existence of some exponent. All numeric carriers and power instances are Nat."
    },
    {
      "scope": "XT02-03 / public ordinals25-29",
      "assessment": "Universal log/clog bounds are nonstrict with actual numLeaves. AlmostComplete is the sole shape premise of both exact rounded formulae. height_optimal exports independent payload universes, AlmostComplete only for s, and numNodes s <= numNodes t as its second premise. The competitor needs no invariant; the source proof retains leaves = nodes+1."
    },
    {
      "scope": "XT02-04 / public ordinals30-36",
      "assessment": "All seven actual claims use Real.logb at real literal base2, casts of actual minHeight/height/numLeaves, and Nat.floor/Nat.ceil for the rounded formulae. Universal comparisons have no extra premise, strict comparisons require incompleteness, complete equality requires Complete, and floor/ceil equalities require AlmostComplete. All are exact unchanged public statements after the proof corrections."
    },
    {
      "scope": "XT02-05 / all54 example public ordinals37-90",
      "assessment": "Concrete Unit, Nat and Bool fixtures retain intended types and numbers; the Empty cases are genuinely universally quantified over BinaryTree Empty. RightTwo has strict real comparisons and nonstrict-rounded equality/non-strictness counterexamples. The sample has five leaves/minimum2/height3 and exposes both correct nodes+1 and failure of unshifted nodes. Pair erasure remains cross-universe; mapped sample is genuinely noninjective. Corrupt shape remains independent of Valid. Minimum reader has the exact recursive Valid 0 minStep premise; annotated sample has actual validity/erase/read laws. Boolean optimum counter and arbitrary-payload competitor theorem retain useful inhabited witnesses. The private recursive sibling predicate is explicitly present in the exported balance theorem. Chains assert only universal rounded bounds."
    }
  ],
